From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:16:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 103/342] kernel debug level 1 (measuring; to keep or revert)

KDEBUG_LEVEL 2 turns on paranoid malloc and free, spinlock and page
access debugging, heap debugging, kernel ASSERTs and TCP's buffer queue
verification; Haiku's own comment says it "will impact performance".
A TCP send on the ODROID-C2 spent about a third of its time in the slab
allocator and the TCP verification. Level 1 keeps the lightweight checks
(the debug syslog, block cache and interrupt debugging).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 build/config_headers/kernel_debug_config.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/build/config_headers/kernel_debug_config.h b/build/config_headers/kernel_debug_config.h
index 404cb94e48..a3c598b9e5 100644
--- a/build/config_headers/kernel_debug_config.h
+++ b/build/config_headers/kernel_debug_config.h
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 // 0: Disables all debug code that hasn't been enabled otherwise.
 // 1: Enables some lightweight debug code.
 // 2: Enables more debug code. Will impact performance.
-#define KDEBUG_LEVEL 2
+#define KDEBUG_LEVEL 1
 
 #define KDEBUG_LEVEL_2	(KDEBUG_LEVEL >= 2)
 #define KDEBUG_LEVEL_1	(KDEBUG_LEVEL >= 1)
